[Mono] Resolve static virtual methods implemented by the constraining interface

Upstreamable: yes. A Mono bug on every architecture (Android, iOS, wasm, s390x,
ppc64le), not a ppc64le workaround. Paths are relative to src/runtime
(dotnet/runtime layout); the dotnet-core PKGBUILD applies it with
`patch -Np1 -d src/runtime`, after the ELFv2 patch.

Upstream: dotnet/runtime #82217 ("BadImageFormatException when calling static
virtual method in interface"), confirmed still broken in 9.0, closed in 2024 as a
duplicate of #79331. #79331 is a different, reflection-only issue and is still
open. get_method_constrained() is unchanged in dotnet/runtime main as of
September 2026.

Root cause
==========
C# lets an interface implement a static abstract or static virtual member of an
interface it inherits:

    interface IBase    { static abstract R M (); }
    interface IDerived : IBase { static R IBase.M () => ...; }
    class G<T> where T : IBase { R Call () => T.M (); }      // used as G<IDerived>

`T.M ()` compiles to a constrained call. For a constraint type that is an
interface, both get_method_constrained() (metadata/loader.c) and the
MONO_RGCTX_INFO_VIRT_METHOD[_CODE] case of instantiate_info()
(mini/mini-generic-sharing.c) return the declaration unchanged ("we don't learn
anything new by constraining"). That holds for instance methods but not for
static virtuals, where the constraining interface supplies the body. The
declaration of a static abstract method has no body. Observed on Mono 10.0.12:

  - non-shared code:  BadImageFormatException: Method has no body
  - shared generics:  assertion in mini_instantiate_gshared_info (), process abort
  - static virtual with a default body overridden by the derived interface:
    silently calls the base body (wrong result)

CoreCLR resolves all three correctly.

GirCore generates exactly this pattern: every binding interface (for example
Gtk.SelectionModel) implements GObject.GTypeProvider.GetGType(), and
Signal<TSender, TSignalArgs>.GetId() calls TSender.GetGType(). Pinta's
LayersListView connects SelectionModel.OnSelectionChanged while
MainWindow.Activate() builds the window, before the action handlers are
created. The exception therefore leaves every menu action (New, Open, About,
...) without a handler, and it is silent because the error dialog is not
initialised yet either.

Fix
===
mono_class_get_static_virtual_impl_in_interface () searches the constraining
interface and the interfaces it inherits for a MethodImpl whose declaration is
the called static virtual method, preferring the most derived interface. The
two constrained-call paths use it before falling back to the declaration.
Instance methods and class constraint types are unchanged. A generic method's
instantiation is re-applied to the implementation.

Verification
============
A console repro plus nine cases added to the ELFv2 conformance suite:
  - class T implementing the member
  - class T inheriting an interface implementation
  - interface T in shared generic class code, twice
  - interface T in a generic method
  - GirCore's Signal shape
  - static virtual default body
  - one-level and two-level interface overrides
Stock Mono 10.0.12: 3 aborts, 1 BadImageFormatException, 2 wrong results.
Patched: all correct. The 50 ABI cases are unchanged. Pinta's New and Open
actions work where they silently did nothing.

